topics/harmonic-form.content:
Given
\begin{align}
a\sin x + b\cos x \equiv R\sin(x+\alpha)
\end{align}
then
\begin{align}
R^2 &amp;=a^2+b^2 &amp; \tan\alpha &amp;=\dfrac{b}{a}\\
R &amp;= \sqrt{a^2 + b^2} &amp; \alpha &amp;= \arctan\dfrac{b}{a}
\end{align}

topics/integrating-miscellaneous-trig-fu.content:
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \cos^3 x \sin^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int \cos x (1 - \sin^2 x) \sin^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int \cos x (\sin^2 x - \sin^4 x) \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int \cos x \sin^2 x - \cos x \sin^4 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \dfrac{1}{3}\sin^3 x - \dfrac{1}{5}\sin^5 x + c
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \dfrac{\sin x}{\cos^2 x} \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int \sec x \tan x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \sec x + c
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \dfrac{\cos x}{\sin^2 x} \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int \text{cosec} x \cot x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ -\text{cosec} x + c
\end{align}
