topics/integrating-squared-trig-function.content:
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \sin^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int\dfrac{1 - \cos 2x}{2} \text{ d}x \\
=&amp;\ \dfrac{x}{2} - \dfrac{\sin 2x}{4} + c 
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \cos^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\int\dfrac{1 + \cos 2x}{2} \text{ d}x \\
=&amp;\ \dfrac{x}{2} + \dfrac{\sin 2x}{4} + c 
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \tan^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \sec^2 x - 1 \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \tan x - x + c
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \cot^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \text{cosec}^2 x - 1 \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ -\cot x - x + c
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \sec^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp;\ \tan x + c
\end{align}
\begin{align}
&amp;\int \text{cosec}^2 x \text{ d}x\\
=&amp; -\cot x + c
\end{align}
